  "spoken": "Not all the dinosaurs died. When the asteroid struck sixty-six million years ago, a few small feathered ones survived. Their descendants are all around you now: the pigeon on the pavement, the robin in the garden, the gull at the seaside. Every bird you have ever seen is a living dinosaur. Look up. They never really left",
